{# ============================================================
   SCIENCE: Bonfire for research communities.

   THIS PAGE IS A SHOP WINDOW, NOT A SPECIFICATION.
   It does not replace openscience.network. Two audiences:
   non-scientists, who should learn Bonfire serves researchers
   and click nothing; and scientists, who should get thirsty and
   click through to OSN. So: teasers, quotes, name-drops and
   links, NOT explanatory prose. If a reader finishes this page
   feeling they now know everything, it has failed. Every claim
   ends in a destination. When in doubt, hand off.

   Content framing is inherited from the `research` recipe in
   _includes/v2/recipes.njk (the homepage Community Fit Explorer):
   same corn accent, same starts/blocks/becomes argument, same
   block list. If that recipe changes, change this to match, and
   never claim as shipped anything the recipe flags `soon: true`.

   Class vocabulary is the current house style, shared with
   features.njk / compare.njk / vs-mastodon.njk.

   NAMING REAL PEOPLE AND INSTITUTIONS, so:
   · Every partner description must be one they'd endorse. Say
     what they do and state the connection plainly; never imply
     endorsement of Bonfire that hasn't been given.
   · Bonfire is a PARTNER on PROVIDES, not the lead, and it is a
     scoping phase with no findings yet. Do not upgrade it.
   · open_science.md (2023) is a funding PROPOSAL. Preprints,
     Crossref DOIs, journals-as-groups, editor roles and review
     badging are all proposed there, not built. Don't mine it.
   · Publications are other people's work. Authors, venue, year,
     and the DOI where there is one.
   ============================================================ #}

