  <div class="relative z-[1]">

    {# ---------- hero ---------- #}
    <header class="pt-10 pb-[clamp(40px,5vw,60px)]">
    <div class="max-w-[1140px] mx-auto px-7">
      <h1 class="mt-[22px] font-disp font-semibold text-[clamp(2.1rem,5vw,3.7rem)] leading-[1.05] tracking-[-.02em] text-balance max-w-[20ch] [font-variation-settings:'opsz'_96]">Open science infrastructure, shaped by the communities who rely on it.</h1>

      <p class="mt-[36px] text-[1.08rem] text-ink-2 max-w-[62ch] [&_b]:text-ink [&_b]:font-semibold">Bonfire partners with universities, scholarly networks and science communicators who <b>run spaces</b> of their own, <b>co-design around real practice</b>, and <b>research how communities actually work</b>, such as experimenting with new forms of governance and open knowledge exchange.</p>

      <p class="mt-5 text-[1.08rem] text-ink-2 max-w-[62ch]">Our collaborations span living labs at Warwick, governance research with Princeton HCI and design experiments with the Prosocial Design Network, and together they shape the <a class="text-spark hover:underline" href="https://openscience.network" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open Science Network</a>, a scholarly edition of Bonfire. The code, design patterns and methods we develop return to the commons, openly licensed.</p>

      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3.5 mt-9">
        <a class="{{ btnfire }}" href="#who">Explore our collaborations</a>
        <a class="{{ btnline }}" href="/contact">Propose a collaboration</a>
      </div>
    </div></header>

    <main>

