    {# ---------- the Open Science Network ---------- #}
    <section id="osn" class="py-[clamp(56px,7vw,96px)] border-t border-ink/[0.07] scroll-mt-[70px]">
    <div class="max-w-[1140px] mx-auto px-7">
      <p class="{{ eyebrow }}"><i class="w-[9px] h-[9px] flex-none bg-[var(--acc)] [clip-path:polygon(50%_0,100%_50%,50%_100%,0_50%)]" aria-hidden="true"></i>The Open Science Network</p>
      <h2 class="{{ display }}">Bonfire, assembled <span class="corn-text">for scholarship.</span></h2>
      <p class="mt-5 text-[1.02rem] text-ink-2 max-w-[44rem]">The Open Science Network is a ready-made set of building blocks, put together for research and governed by the researchers who use it, shaped with the scholarly organisations above. It's a starting point rather than a finished product: every community that takes it up reshapes it. <a class="text-spark hover:underline" href="https://www.univ-lorraine.fr/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Université de Lorraine</a> and the Paris region digital university network (<a class="text-spark hover:underline" href="https://unif.fr" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">UNIF</a>) are among the institutions lining up next. A university, a scholarly society, a lab or a collective can each run its own server, shaped to meet their needs, and stay connected to all the others.</p>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-6 gap-3.5 mt-[34px]">
        {%- for f in osn.included %}
        <div class="{{ cell }} !p-0 overflow-hidden lg:col-span-{{ f.span }}">
          <img class="h-56 w-full object-cover {{ f.pos }}" src="{{ f.img }}" alt="" loading="lazy">
